Paninda revision 005 — sync presentation, light system chrome and rotating Home copy
Date: 2026-11-05 (UTC)
Branch: litmus_2
Base: 441863f

REQUEST
Successful sync should show a checkmark, Home subtitle should show last sync via
separate getter logic, system navigation controls should remain visible in the
light-only app, and time-based microcopy should rotate across app launches.

IMPLEMENTED
- Added domain/model/SyncStatus.kt: a read-only ShopState.syncSummary getter with
  typed phases, pending count and lastSuccessfulAt. A persisted success status
  without an actual timestamp is treated as Ready, not a fabricated success.
  Pending changes and failures/conflicts retain the last successful timestamp.
- SyncStatusScreen uses CheckCircle after successful sync, Sync for pending/
  in-progress work, a neutral cloud for Ready, and WarningAmber only for actual
  failures, access/format issues or conflicts. Existing monochrome palette kept.
- ui/sync/SyncPresentation.kt centralizes status labels and last-sync formatting
  for Home, Sync Status and Settings. Date plus time uses the shop's Manila zone;
  missing history reads "Last sync: Never". No API call occurs in the getter.
  The existing internal lastCheckedAt field/key still holds completed-sync time;
  no Room schema migration or new successful timestamp is introduced.
- Home subtitle now uses last sync, replacing the static LOCAL FIRST label.
- Removed the leftover values-night native theme, which selected a dark window
  and light controls even though Compose always renders light. MainActivity now
  explicitly requests light system-bar styling/dark status/navigation controls,
  independent of device dark mode. Pre-26 devices use the supported dark scrim
  fallback where dark navigation controls are unavailable.
- Added ui/home/Microcopies.kt and strings_microcopies.xml containing all 19
  supplied phrases. Corrected obvious "RIse" and "Gridning" typos only.
  Manila-time pools: morning 05:00–10:59, lunch 11:00–12:59, afternoon 13:00–16:59,
  evening 17:00–21:59, late night 22:00–04:59.
- A single application-scoped rotation instance caches the selection for each
  time period. SharedPreferences remembers each pool's last index across cold
  launches, cycling without repeats until the pool wraps. Returning to Home,
  recomposing or recreating the activity does not advance the phrase. A lifecycle-
  aware minute check updates the pool while Home is visible and on resume.
- Updated the existing navigation behavior smoke check to locate Home by its
  sync action instead of the removed static subtitle. Added two focused tests
  for success/pending/failure getters and time boundaries/launch rotation.
- No maintained layout tests, screenshot baselines or device-size matrix added.

VERIFICATION
- Build, lint and 18 maintained focused checks are being run; results below.
- System gesture/button appearance still benefits from acceptance on the target
  physical device/OEM. No emulator/device screenshot claim is made.

FINAL CHECKS
- assembleDebug + lintDebug completed successfully. Android lint: 0 errors.
- All 18 maintained regression checks passed (0 failures/errors), including the
  existing navigation/product behavior smoke check with the dynamic Home header.
- Debug APK: app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk. No remote Git push or Drive
